# SDL2 testautomation oracle

Source pin: SDL `release-2.30.11`, commit `fa24d868ac2f8fd558e4e914c9863411245db8fd`. The vendored upstream sources are `test/testautomation_pixels.c` and `test/testautomation_surface.c`; `test/harness.c` only selects those two original suites. Upstream SDL test code is under the zlib license in `test/COPYING` (copyright/license header retained in each source).

Build the two suites and `test/harness.c` as a 32-bit i386 ELF against SDL 2.30.11 and its matching `SDL2_test` library. It must run natively with the same i386 SDL2 shared library and run through `test/elfconv/run_i386.py --source <compiled-suite-source>` after the runner supports those link flags. Use `SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy` only if SDL initialization requests video; this focused harness initializes SDL without subsystems. Keep the test working directory writable: the upstream surface save/load test creates and deletes `testSaveLoadBitmap.bmp`.

## Coverage map

| Behavior | Existing upstream oracle | Adaptation | Runtime modes | Gaps |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Pixel-format metadata across SDL2 formats, invalid formats, palette lifecycle, gamma ramp, names | `pixels_allocFreeFormat`, `pixels_allocFreePalette`, `pixels_calcGammaRamp`, `pixels_getPixelFormatName` in `testautomation_pixels.c` | Harness chooses `pixelsTestSuite` unchanged | Native i386 SDL2 and lifted run require matching SDL2 `SDL2_test` build and linked runtime | Does not test per-pixel map/get conversion values; SDL2 release suite has no mapping/conversion case in this file. |
| Surface conversion, indexed/packed formats, surface load/save, format/pitch overflow validation | `surface_testSurfaceConversion`, `surface_testCompleteSurfaceConversion`, `surface_testSaveLoadBitmap`, `surface_testOverflow` in `testautomation_surface.c` | Harness selects the upstream `surfaceTestSuite` unchanged | Same SDL2 i386 build and shared runner | Overflow checks validate bad/undersized pitch inputs but do not prove pixel traversal on valid padded pitch. |
| Nonuniform surface blit, color modulation, alpha modulation, clipping/placement | `surface_testBlit`, `surface_testBlitColorMod`, `surface_testBlitAlphaMod`, `surface_testBlitBlendNone`; expected images are produced by SDL2_test's `SDLTest_Image*` fixtures and compared with `SDLTest_CompareSurfaces` | Suite unchanged; link matching `SDL2_test` for its images/comparator | Same SDL2 i386 build and shared runner | Blend, add, and alpha-blit reference cases are marked `TEST_DISABLED` in this release. These are software-surface tests, not renderer or window tests. |
| Audio lifecycle and callback behavior | SDL2 upstream `testautomation_audio.c`: `audio_quitInitAudio`, `audio_initQuitAudio`, `audio_initOpenCloseQuitAudio`, `audio_pauseUnpauseAudio` | Not included in this focused executable | Could be selected separately with a dummy audio driver and matching SDL2 library | Requires actual SDL2 audio backend; does not prove callback TLS or general thread-local storage semantics. |
| Event push/filter/poll and userdata | SDL2 `testautomation_events.c`: `events_pushPumpAndPollUserevent`, `events_addDelEventWatch`, `events_addDelEventWatchWithUserdata` | Not included | Requires matching SDL2 library; event subsystem may be used headless | No comprehensive event ABI coverage. |
| Video window/display behavior | SDL2 `testautomation_video.c` | Not included | Needs an actual usable video driver/display and matching SDL2 runtime; dummy-driver success does not cover platform windows | Does not establish Portal compatibility. |
| Renderer operations | SDL2 `testautomation_render.c`: enabled primitive/blit tests; blend and alpha cases `render_testPrimitivesBlend`, `render_testBlitAlpha`, and `render_testBlitBlend` are disabled | Not included | Requires an actual renderer; tests depend on SDL automation window setup | Renderer tests do not establish dynamic OpenGL thunk correctness, orientation, depth, alpha, ordering, or GL import behavior. |
| Window manager info | SDL2 `testautomation_syswm.c`: `syswm_getWindowWMInfo` | Not included | Platform window system required | Does not establish SDL_GetWindowWMInfo Portal compatibility. |

## Integration requirements

`run_i386.py --source` compiles one source with `-lm` only. Main integration must add a way to pass SDL2 include/link flags and the matching `SDL2_test`/SDL2 shared-library dependencies to the i386 compile, ensure native loader search path resolves the i386 SDL2 build, and make those same host SDL2 shared libraries available to the lifted runtime's SDL adapters. Run each executable independently through the existing native/lifted comparison runner; native failures remain failures, not expected-output baselines. Do not modify GL imports as part of this test slice.
